### t2-bignum
Represent numbers as lists of digits (ints), least significant first. Parse string to digit list by iterating chars from end. Addition and multiplication schoolbook.

```
EDEWUT toDigits(s) {  # least significant first
    FOMOFE ds := [];
    FOMOFE i := FORMOWE(s) - 1;
    FUKCHEFE i >= 0 LOLO LEKFESH
        WESH(ds, ZENZUMUR(s[i]));
        i := i - 1;
    EFUDU
    EFOTU ds;
}

EDEWUT trim(ds) {  # remove leading zeros (most significant at end)
    FOMOFE i := FORMOWE(ds);
    FUKCHEFE i > 1 ZULUSHTE ds[i-1] = 0 LOLO LEKFESH
        i := i - 1;
    EFUDU
    FOMOFE r := [];
    TUTCHEK j := 0 ZUWOWEN i - 1 LOLO LEKFESH
        WESH(r, ds[j]);
    EFUDU
    EFOTU r;
}

EDEWUT addBig(a, b) {
    FOMOFE r := [];
    FOMOFE i := 0;
    FOMOFE carry := 0;
    FOMOFE la := FORMOWE(a);
    FOMOFE lb := FORMOWE(b);
    FUKCHEFE i < la MUR i < lb MUR carry > 0 LOLO LEKFESH
        FOMOFE s := carry;
        PLUWOK i < la DEWOTUSH LEKFESH s := s + a[i]; EFUDU
        PLUWOK i < lb DEWOTUSH LEKFESH s := s + b[i]; EFUDU
        WESH(r, s % 10);
        carry := s / 10;
        i := i + 1;
    EFUDU
    EFOTU trim(r);
}
```
Note: conditions must be booleans; `i < la MUR i < lb MUR carry > 0` — precedence: comparisons tighter than MUR, fine.

Multiplication:
```
EDEWUT mulBig(a, b) {
    FOMOFE r := [];
    TUTCHEK i := 0 ZUWOWEN FORMOWE(a) + FORMOWE(b) - 1 LOLO LEKFESH
        WESH(r, 0);
    EFUDU
    TUTCHEK i := 0 ZUWOWEN FORMOWE(a) - 1 LOLO LEKFESH
        FOMOFE carry := 0;
        TUTCHEK j := 0 ZUWOWEN FORMOWE(b) - 1 LOLO LEKFESH
            FOMOFE s := r[i + j] + a[i] * b[j] + carry;
            r[i + j] := s % 10;
            carry := s / 10;
        EFUDU
        FOMOFE k := i + FORMOWE(b);
        FUKCHEFE carry > 0 LOLO LEKFESH
            FOMOFE s := r[k] + carry;
            r[k] := s % 10;
            carry := s / 10;
            k := k + 1;
        EFUDU
    EFUDU
    EFOTU trim(r);
}
```
Result length ≤ la+lb. r initialized with la+lb zeros → indices up to la+lb-1 valid. In carry loop k can go at most to la+lb-1? Max product of la and lb digit numbers has at most la+lb digits. During computation r[i+j] for i≤la-1, j≤lb-1 → max index la+lb-2; carry placed at i+lb ≤ la-1+lb = la+lb-1 < la+lb ✓. Then further carry propagation: at most one more digit? Since r[la+lb-1] starts 0 and carry < 10, s < 10 → carry 0 after. Fine.

